From 20eb7ab75aa3ffe9092bcb4b06ccd6f85e588d3e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 08:08:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Logging accordion follow-ups: rotation, JSON/INFO defaults,
 restart notice, reorder

- Log rotation: optional Max file size / Files to keep / Keep for fields
  (Caddy's roll_size/roll_keep/roll_keep_for), left blank to use Caddy's
  own defaults (100MiB / 10 files / 2160h). Files to keep is validated
  as a positive whole number when set. Rendering nests `output file`
  into its own block only when at least one rotation option is set,
  otherwise it stays the bare single line as before.
- extract_logging's fallback parser now finds the `log` block's actual
  matching closing brace (via a small brace-depth counter) instead of a
  non-greedy regex, since the nested `output file { ... }` block for
  rotation options meant the old regex could stop at the wrong `}`.
  Rotation values round-trip through it too.
- JSON/INFO are now the pre-selected defaults in both dropdowns
  (previously Console/INFO), matching Caddy's own default format for a
  non-terminal (file) output.
- Added an info line inside the Logging accordion noting Caddy must be
  reloaded/restarted for logging changes to take effect.
- Swapped accordion order per feedback: Advanced options now comes
  before Logging in all five block types (it was the reverse before).

Verified: caddyfile.py unit checks (render_log_block defaults/rotation
nesting, extract_logging round-tripping rotation values and finding
level/format past the nested brace), full Flask test-client coverage
(rotation fields end to end, invalid roll_keep surfaces an error and
doesn't write a file, blank rotation stays a bare output line, JSON
pre-selected with Console not selected, Advanced-before-Logging DOM
order) across all five block types, and the full prior regression
suite (create/edit/rename/delete/disable-deletes-file) still passes.
pyflakes clean.
